 "researcher_notes": "Not an existing row: roster has no ANR WestLeg or Madison/Beloit Lateral row (ANR rows P0152 main line, P2501, P2530, P3187 Wisconsin Access, P4380, P5547 Wisconsin Reliability, P6584, P7793 Heartland are different projects). ANR Pipeline Co (El Paso Corp unit) applied to FERC Sept 2002 (docket CP02-434 per search result, not verified by url_verifier): 26.3 mi of 30 in loop on Madison Lateral (McHenry County IL, Walworth and Rock Counties WI) plus 6.5 mi of 20 in replacing 4 in and 6 in Beloit Lateral pipes in Rock County WI; 220 Mdth/d added; $42.1 million. Length 32.8 mi total (26.3 loop is new pipe, 6.5 mi replacement is mostly like-for-like; both well above 15.5 mi threshold either way). Passes add-threshold: sponsor, endpoints, FERC application. STATUS NOT STAGED: search results say FERC certificate 6/5/2003 and in service Oct/Nov 2004, but the only sources found for that are the banned abarrelfull page and unverified snippets; no citable page confirming approval or in-service was found. Likely operating, reviewer should confirm via FERC order (docket CP02-434) or ANR 10-K. Build year is therefore 2003-2004 not 2003. Route: not researched, no GIS found; Madison lateral loop parallels existing 10 and 12 in lines. Capacity 220 Mdth/d is dekatherms per day, staged as stated. Owner styled via entity_style (ANR Pipeline Co, El Paso Corp; both exist in the gas gazetteer). Tier medium: sources are two independent-ish trade press items plus a Federal Register notice that restate the same FERC application (one origin)."
